With several acclaimed roles under his belt, Mahershala Ali still finds himself on equal footing in many casting rooms.

The 2x Academy Award winner recently explained that having the Oscar statuettes "doesn't matter" in casting conversations, explaining that the coveted acting honor is "kind of just talk" and "doesn't translate to anything real."

"It's a natural way for people to think. But on some level, what does an Oscar mean? It's an award, and it's an award where you're being recognized, hopefully for doing good work. But there's a lot of great actors that don't have Oscars , who are also looking for good material. So, it doesn't really mean anything. And that's no disrespect to The Academy or the award at all, but what I'm actually saying is that, Oscar or no Oscar, there's a lot of good actors out there," he explained on the 7pm in Brooklyn podcast. "There's more good actors than there is good material." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Ali continued, "And it's not even that all these people are competing for these same spots. It's just that out of all the material made, there's only a handful of them that check certain boxes. And then you got to be right for it. Just because a script is good doesn't mean that I'm right for it or whoever wrote it is thinking about me, of all people. So, who is centered? The vast majority of projects that get greenlit, there are not roles for me in those. You gotta think that way, you know what I mean? So, it doesn't matter if I got 17 Oscars. If someone is not writing something for you or greenlighting something with you in mind, you're like everybody else waiting and looking and searching." Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Noting that rollbacks of Diversity, Equity and Inclusion (DEI) programs "on some level impact what gets greenlit," Ali explained "that if certain companies are allowed to not feel a pressure to be reflective of the world we live in, they'll just keep centering who they see in their offices, and it ain't a bunch of us in those offices."

At the same time, Ali doesn't want to be typecast in another "diversity project," adding, "You just want to do great material as a Black person. You're not thinking of yourself as this exotic other, per se. You just are living your life. You wake up. You put your pants on like everybody else. You just want to be like, 'Yo, this is my offering. This is my story. This is my work.' Opposed to, 'Man, who are the best Black actors?'" blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

With Ali earning Oscar buzz for his latest starring role in Bassam Tariq's Y our Mother Your Mother Your Mother , the actor previously won Best Supporting Actor for Moonlight in 2017 and Green Book in 2019.

Chris Colfer is opening up about what it meant to play his now-beloved &#x201C; Glee &#x201D; character, Kurt Hummel, a month after reuniting on stage with his on-screen love interest and co-star, Darren Criss.

Criss (who played Blaine Anderson on the hit show) and Colfer surprised audiences by performing &#x201C;Baby It&#x2019;s Cold Outside,&#x201D; an homage to their "Glee" characters, during the &#x201C;American Crime Story&#x201D; actor&#x2019;s London concert on Oct. 18. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories CMAs Photo Gallery: See Taylor Swift, Ella Langley, Kacey Musgraves, Lainey Wilson, Stella Lefty and Other Stars on the Carpet and On-Stage Celluloid Sounds: Fewer Women Composers on Screen, But Some Hit the Right Notes

Speaking with People about the evening, Colfer said it &#x201C;was a really special night for me.&#x201D; &#x201C;We had been planning it for months. I was not expecting the reaction that we got,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;I was expecting a few hoots and hollers, maybe a couple of gasps, but I was never expecting to get a standing ovation at Royal Albert Hall.&#x201D;

Colfer added that the reception was &#x201C;really healing, honestly.&#x201D; He continued: "Because of the homophobia and hatred that I was exposed to at such a young age during the show, and because of the hatred that the show has received since it stopped airing, I had kind of forgotten that that character meant so much to people. So it was a really, really nice reminder, and I think it was a life highlight for me.&#x201D;

Colfer has long been outspoken about the bullying he endured while on the show, and in 2024, even revealed he was warned not to come out as gay . &#x201C;When I started filming the show, I had a lot of people tell me, &#x2018;Do not come out whatever you do because it will ruin your career.&#x2019; So I hid for a little bit,&#x201D; he said during an appearance on &#x201C;The View.&#x201D; &#x201C;But I also told them, &#x2018;I can&#x2019;t hide it with my voice&#x2026; I&#x2019;m more effeminate than most people. I can&#x2019;t hide it.&#x2019; And they said, &#x2018;Don&#x2019;t worry. As long as you never address it, you&#x2019;ll be rewarded for it in the end.&#x2019;&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Just days after Colfer and Criss&#x2019; performance, news broke that Disney+ and Hulu had greenlit a reboot of Ryan Murphy&#x2019;s musical dramedy series. While Variety reported that original cast member Lea Michele is set to return as Rachel Berry, Colfer has been more ambiguous about his involvement, though he did recently confirm on The Daily Beast&#x2019;s &#x201C;Obsessed: The Podcast&#x201D; that he is having conversations about reprising his role. &#x201C;From what I heard, it sounded very funny, and it sounded like a good idea. So we&#x2019;ll see,&#x201D; he said.

Spain&#x2019;s Huelva Ibero-American Film Festival , one of Europe&#x2019;s foremost Latin American cinema platforms, prized two of the region&#x2019;s cinema greats, awarding top prizes to Chilean actor Alfredo Castro and Argentine writer-director Luc&#xED;a Puenzo on Saturday night.

&#x201C; La Bola Negra &#x201D; also reaped yet another plaudit, its scribe-helmer-producer duo Javier Calvo and Javier Ambrossi - Los Javis &#x2013; scoring Best Spanish Direction. Related Stories Ella Langley Breaks a CMA Awards Record by Winning Six in One Night, Including Entertainer of the Year: The Complete List of Winners CMAs Photo Gallery: See Taylor Swift, Ella Langley, Kacey Musgraves, Lainey Wilson, Stella Lefty and Other Stars on the Carpet and On-Stage

Huelva&#x2019;s prizes highlight the festival&#x2019;s focus under director Manuel H. Mart&#xED;n on crossover films, often mixing genre-bending and social issues to surprising effect. Top winner &#x201C;After Elena.&#x201D; from Chile's Shawn Garry, turns on mourning but is a comedy; Luc&#xED;a Puenzo&#x2019;s &#x201C;Pepita, the Gunslinger&#x201D; is a gangster movie but the gangster is a woman who battles corruption. &#x201C;Funk,&#x201D; which won Duda Santos best actress, is a musical but &#x201C;revolutionary,&#x201D; says director Aly Muritiba , in its centering &#x201C;Black joy.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The 2026 awards also may be the gayest in Huelva&#x2019;s history, with nearly half going to LGBT movies in a year where Variety has asked whether the 2026-27 Oscars season is their gayest ever.

The double nods for the Shawn Garry directed &#x201C;After Elena&#x201D;(&#x201C;Despu&#xE9;s de Elena&#x201D;) also underscore what Huelva does best: Highlighting titles that deserve further recognition which in the case of Latin America includes most of its movies, given they are under-covered by the international media.

A TIFF world premiere sold by Meikincine and lead produced by Gabriela Sandoval out of her Cine Matriz label, &#x201C;After Elena&#x201D; is not just a study of grief but also a family dynamics comedy with the children of Roberto, 70, moving into his home to supposedly to look after him but also to get their hands on his wife and their mother Elena&#x2019;s inheritance. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Sluiced by a playful irony, &#x201C;After Elena&#x201D; took home Huelva&#x2019;s Golden Columbus and Best Actor for Castro, once described by Variety as &#x201C;reliably superb&#x201D; though here acting against type, abandoning the &#x201C;heightened performances I&#x2019;m used to&#x201D; for &#x201C;strict, grounded realism,&#x201D; he told Variety .

Luc&#xED;a Puenzo, the celebrated Argentine auteur (&#x201C;XXY&#x201D;) and pioneer of Latin American premium TV (&#x201C;La Jaur&#xED;a,&#x201D; &#x201C;Se&#xF1;orita 89&#x201D;) scored Best Director for &#x201C;Pepita, the Gunslinger,&#x201D; which reflects one of the things she does best: Wrapping gender-agenda issues in engrossing thriller narratives. Here Luisana Lopilato (&#x201C;In Love and in Hate&#x201D;) plays the real-life Margarita Di Tullio who rebelled against the deaths of fellow sex workers in 1980s Mar del Plata by founding her own brothel and nightlife business empire.

&#x201C;La Bola Negra&#x2019;s&#x201D; Best Spanish Direction Award in Huelva&#x2019;s Acento Cine Espa&#xF1;ol section marks the latest recognition from Los Javis&#x2019; native Spain, which scored the San Sebasti&#xE1;n Festival Audience Award and has grossed a massive &#x20AC;40.4 million ($44.4 million) through Nov. 22, passing &#x201C;Spider-Man: Brand New Day&#x201D; to become the highest-grossing movie of any nationality in Spain his year, according to Rentrak Spain

Allan Deberton's &#x201C;Gugu&#x2019;s World,&#x201D; Brazil&#x2019;s crowdpleasing International Feature Oscar entry nabbed Huelva&#x2019;s Audience Award, adding to other kudos such as a Berlin Generation Plus Crystal Bear and Guadalajara Maguey Best Film Award.

Spain&#x2019;s Rub&#xE9;n Ochandiano (&#x201C;Broken Embraces&#x201D;) scooped Best Supporting Actor for his performance as a musician who galvanizes the protagonist&#x2019;s life in Mexican Lorena Villarreal&#x2019;s &#x201C;Life Is&#x201D; (&#x201C;La Vida Es&#x201D;).

Elsewhere, Huelva&#x2019;s awards spotlighted disparate talents to track. Sharon Kleinberg's &#x201C;I Am Mario&#x201D; walked off with Huelva&#x2019;s Special Jury Prize. It turns on Mario, a forty-year-old trans taxi driver who faces an unexpected pregnancy which fulfils his dream to become a father but shatters some of his beliefs about masculinity. &#x201C;I Am Mario&#x201D; also won at Guadalajara Film Fest&#x2019;s Maguey section , scooping its Jury Award in April.

